\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For a smooth connected rationally connected complex projective X with holomorphic $T_X=V_{1}\oplus V_{2}$, must both summands be integrable and X be biholomorphic to a product whose two factor tangents correspond to the given summands?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For a smooth connected rationally connected complex projective X with holomorphic $T_X=V_{1}\oplus V_{2}$, must both summands be integrable and X be biholomorphic to a product whose two factor tangents correspond to the given summands?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.08814}.
\item[S2] Original question source or mathematical context.
